+++++++++++++++++++++++++++Verification blank report++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

t can be normal or it can mean your report query is returning zero rows because of filters / action_id mismatch / wrong audit file path. The fastest way to know is to run 3 checks.

1) Confirm the audit view is actually returning rows

Run:

SELECT TOP (20) *
FROM dbo.v_Audit_All
ORDER BY event_time DESC;

If this returns 0 rows

Then the weekly email will be blank because the base view is empty. Common causes:

wrong audit file path in sys.fn_get_audit_file

SQL Server service account can’t read the folder/share

audit is writing somewhere else

✅ Fix: correct the path and permissions.

2) Confirm your audit contains the event types you expect

Run:

SELECT TOP (50) action_id, COUNT(*) AS cnt
FROM dbo.v_Audit_All
WHERE event_time >= DATEADD(DAY,-7, SYSUTCDATETIME())
GROUP BY action_id
ORDER BY cnt DESC;

If you don’t see expected action_ids like:

SL (SELECT)

LGIF (login failed) (depends on what you enabled)

DR/DL (drop) (depends on what you enabled)

Then your view may be fine, but your filters don’t match the actual action_id codes in your audit.

✅ Fix: adjust the report views/proc to use the action_ids you actually have.

3) Confirm the weekly report procedure has data to print

Before sending the email, verify the same timeframe:

DECLARE @StartDT DATETIME2(7) = '2026-02-16';
DECLARE @EndDT   DATETIME2(7) = '2026-02-23';

SELECT COUNT(*) AS TotalInWindow
FROM dbo.v_Audit_All
WHERE event_time >= @StartDT AND event_time < @EndDT;

SELECT COUNT(*) AS SelectsInWindow
FROM dbo.v_Audit_All
WHERE event_time >= @StartDT AND event_time < @EndDT
  AND action_id = 'SL';


If TotalInWindow = 0 → base is empty → report blank.

If TotalInWindow > 0 but SelectsInWindow = 0 → SELECT auditing isn’t captured (or action_id differs).

Why “blank email” happens even when things are working

Even if events exist, your email body can still appear blank if:

You’re building HTML but sections only render when there are rows, and all sections are empty

The procedure doesn’t include “No events found” text

FOR XML PATH returns NULL and you don’t print fallback text (common)

✅ Fix: add explicit “No findings this period” blocks so the email is never empty.

Quick Fix (make email never blank)

In your email procedure, add a final safeguard:

IF @html IS NULL OR LEN(@html) < 500
BEGIN
    SET @html = N'<h2>Weekly Audit Pack - TERA</h2>'
              + N'<p>No qualifying audit events were found for this period (or filters excluded all events).</p>';
END

